{"lean":{"expected":false,"path":null,"via":null,"ref":null},"qa":{"label":"prf:noble-gas-characterization","kind":"proof","sidecar":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/noble-gas-characterization-proof.qa.json","counts":{"pass":41,"bad":0,"na":17,"other":0,"stale":1},"criteria":[{"id":"trap-closing-aphorism","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-em-dash","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-meta-commentary","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-negation-contrast","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"pass on all ten trap criteria. THREE FINDINGS, none fixed inline. (1) A PROPOSITION PROVED FROM A CONJECTURE, invisible to the manifest. The reverse direction says in so many words 'follows from the shell conjecture'. The natural referent in the corpus is conj:electron-shell-2n2-capacity. Neither this proof's uses[] (['prop:noble-gas-characterization']) nor the proposition's uses[] (['rem:helium-hopf-diagram']) declares any conj: label, so the conjectural-propagation audit of AGENTS.md 3b cannot see the dependency \u2014 and 3b requires a block downstream of a conjecture to be a conjecture, or to satisfy the 3b-cond conditional-class exception with the conjecture named in uses[] and carried as an explicit instance hypothesis. Neither holds here. Proposed: name the conjecture with a link, add it to uses[], and either demote the proposition or state it conditionally. (2) UNRESOLVED CITATION: 'the Hopf stability proposition' is given without a label. The only Hopf-stability result in the corpus is prop:torus-hopf-stability, 'Torus knot composites on Bring's surface are stable hadrons' \u2014 a statement about HADRONS, not about electron sub-Hopf links, so either the citation points somewhere else or the domains do not match. (3) THE REVERSE DIRECTION'S PHYSICAL STEP IS FALSE AS STATED: 'The atom lowers its energy by capturing an additional electron, contradicting chemical inertness.' An open linking site does not imply a favourable electron capture \u2014 nitrogen, magnesium and manganese all have unfilled shells and non-positive electron affinity, and alkali metals react by donating rather than capturing. The argument needs 'gains or loses an electron', or a restriction to atoms with positive electron affinity.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-nonspeakable","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-tr